-- title:
--   Four times the LX diameter equals the integer parity-sensitive quadratic for n at least five
-- statement:
--   Let $n\ge5$, and let $D_n$ be the diameter of the permutation word metric generated by forward cyclic rotation $i\mapsto i+1$ and the adjacent transposition $(0\ 1)$. Equivalently, $D_n$ is the largest minimum word length needed to reach a permutation from the identity. Then
--
--   $$
--   4D_n=3n^2-8n+12-3(n\bmod2).
--   $$
--
--   The equality is an integer identity; the parity remainder is zero for even $n$ and one for odd $n$. This division-free form records the exact diameter and is convenient for comparing integer word-price bounds.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/SharpDiameterAll.lean#L61-L68

